   463	If we moreover have $b>ka_2$ for some $k\geq1$, then
   464	\begin{equation}\label{eq:prva_njdnok_51}
   465	    n<\frac{8\log(1.68068\cdot 10^{14}a_2^3c)\log(0.102665a_2c)}{\log(ka_2c)\log(0.01685a_2^{-3}c)}.
   466	\end{equation}
   467	The right-hand side of the inequality (\ref{eq:prva_njdnok_51}) is decreasing in $c$ when $c>238a_2^3$ which is true in our case. Since $$c>0.25a_1^2b^3>0.0625\cdot k^3a_2^5$$
   468	and $c/b^2>0.0625a_2^2b>6.25\cdot 10^3a_2^2$ we observe the inequality
