   480	\medskip 
   481	\emph{2)} Assume to the contrary, that $c\geq 0.25a_2^2b^3$. It is easy to see that the assumptions of Lemmas \ref{lemma: gornja_n_1} and \ref{lema: donja na n u terminima b i c} are satisfied.
   482	We know from 1) that $a_2>2a_1$, so $a_1'=4(a_2-a_1).$ Also, $\frac{a_2}{2}<a_2-a_1<a_2$. Then 
   483	\begin{align*}
