   669	and the right-hand side is a function decreasing in $c$ since $c>0.0000115^{-1}$. So, we can use a lower bound $c>0.25a_1^2b^3\geq b^3$ in this inequality and obtain $b<1.846\cdot 10^9$. This implies $a_2\leq 42965$. We can improve this upper bound for $a_2$ furthermore by observing for each fixed $a_1\in[8,159]$ a similar inequality with $a_2$. However, for values $a_1\in[2,7]$, this approach yields a larger bound compared to $42965$.   We do a computer search, and it returns there don't exist elements $b$ and $c$ which satisfy all of the conditions. 
